---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Hidden engineering overview. Not linked in navigation, noindex + nofollow,
// excluded from sitemap. Shared by direct link only.

const subdomains = [
  { host: 'wojciech.io', role: 'Public portfolio: insights, case studies, CV, tools', access: 'Public' },
  { host: 'app.wojciech.io', role: 'Private operating workspace', access: 'Password gate' },
  { host: 'gh.wojciech.io', role: 'GrowthHub analytics dashboard', access: 'Password gate' },
  { host: 'academy.wojciech.io', role: 'Academy', access: 'Public' },
  { host: 'notch.wojciech.io', role: 'Notch', access: 'Public' },
  { host: 'subscribe.wojciech.io', role: 'Newsletter funnel', access: 'Public' },
  { host: 'dev (internal)', role: 'Dev dashboard, agent health', access: 'Internal' },
];

const securityChecks = [
  { name: 'Gitleaks secret scan', detail: 'Full git history, every PR + weekly cron' },
  { name: 'Dependency audit', detail: 'npm audit, fails on high/critical' },
  { name: 'Semgrep SAST', detail: 'p/default · p/javascript · p/typescript' },
  { name: 'CodeQL', detail: 'Code analysis, push/PR + weekly' },
  { name: 'Content guard', detail: 'Pre-commit + CI + weekly: NDA names, key patterns' },
  { name: 'Sensitive path guard', detail: 'Blocks PRs touching protected paths' },
  { name: 'Security header probe', detail: '6 headers verified across 6 subdomains' },
  { name: 'Branch protection', detail: 'Required checks before merge to main' },
  { name: 'Accessibility (axe)', detail: 'Playwright a11y gate on Chromium + WebKit' },
  { name: 'Lighthouse CI', detail: 'Weekly performance, a11y, SEO audit' },
];

const cardClass = 'rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-[var(--color-border)] p-5';
const h2Class = 'text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1';
const eyebrowClass = 'text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent-hi)] mb-2';
---

<Layout
  title="Engineering & Security Stack · wojciech.io"
  description="Internal engineering overview of wojciech.io and its subdomains: architecture, tooling, CI/CD, security, resilience, and the multi-agent operating model."
  canonical="/stack/"
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-[var(--space-section)]">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-14">
      <p class={eyebrowClass}>Engineering overview · private link</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] tracking-tight mb-4">
        How this is built.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        wojciech.io is one operating system across seven surfaces: an Astro monorepo on
        Cloudflare Pages, with a CI gate, layered security, automated resilience, and a
        multi-agent build model. This page documents the whole thing.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mt-4">Last reviewed: May 2026 · not indexed, not linked in navigation</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-16 text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed">

      <!-- 1. Architecture -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>01 · Architecture</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>One repo, seven surfaces</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          A single npm-workspaces monorepo on <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Astro 6</strong>,
          hosted entirely on <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Static where
          possible, <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Cloudflare Pages Functions</strong> (edge) where
          logic is needed: auth and APIs. One pipeline, seven independently deployed projects.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-6">
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Frontend</p>
            <p class="text-sm">Astro + MDX · Tailwind CSS 4 · CSS custom properties as design tokens · Lenis (smooth scroll) · Motion (animation) · Geist typeface.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Build-time</p>
            <p class="text-sm">OG images via Satori + resvg (SVG to PNG) · Pagefind static search index built post-build · sitemap generation with indexability filter.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-4">
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Shared packages</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              Three internal workspace packages keep the surfaces consistent:
              <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">@wojciech/tokens</code> (design tokens),
              <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">@wojciech/ui</code> (shared components),
              and <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">@wojciech/mdx-components</code> (MDX building blocks).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Infrastructure as code</p>
            <p class="text-sm">Cloudflare Pages projects and custom domains are provisioned with Terraform, with WAF rules documented alongside the config.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Subdomains -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>02 · Surfaces</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Subdomains</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Each surface is its own Cloudflare Pages project, deployed independently.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-[var(--color-border)]">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] px-4 py-3">Domain</th>
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] px-4 py-3">Role</th>
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] px-4 py-3">Access</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {subdomains.map((s) => (
                <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] last:border-0">
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-text)] whitespace-nowrap">{s.host}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3">{s.role}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 whitespace-nowrap text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">{s.access}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Analytics -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>03 · Measurement</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Analytics, consent-gated by default</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Nothing loads before the visitor accepts analytics
          (<code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">cookie-consent === 'accepted'</code>).
          No advertising networks, retargeting pixels, or data brokers.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong><br /><span class="text-sm">Privacy-first, no cookies, always anonymous.</span></li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Google Analytics 4</strong><br /><span class="text-sm">Lazy-loaded after consent, IP anonymised.</span></li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Mixpanel · EU residency</strong><br /><span class="text-sm">Product events: page views, outbound clicks, CTA + newsletter intent.</span></li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">PostHog · EU</strong><br /><span class="text-sm">Product analytics and pageview tracking, loaded only after consent.</span></li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Sentry · EU region</strong><br /><span class="text-sm">Error and performance monitoring.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. i18n -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>04 · Languages</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Internationalisation</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Eight languages in the CV and SEO layer: EN (base), PL, DE, DK, NO, JP, IT, ES. Six fully
          translated homepage locales (de, dk, no, jp, it, es), each with its own
          <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">htmlLang</code>,
          <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-[var(--color-surface-2)] px-1 rounded">hreflang</code>, and OG locale.
          Real translations, not machine output. hreflang and html lang are verified by end-to-end tests.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">Content lives in typed collections: insights, work (case studies), testimonials.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Testing -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>05 · Quality</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Testing</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-3">
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Unit · Vitest</p>
            <p class="text-sm">Middleware CSP, content and locale guards, i18n logic, with coverage.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">End-to-end · Playwright</p>
            <p class="text-sm">Chromium + WebKit: smoke, SEO, hreflang, accessibility (axe), links, critical paths, meta assets. A daily smoke runs against live production.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. CI/CD -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>06 · Delivery</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>CI/CD pipeline</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">1 · CI</strong> on every push and PR to main: build and type-check (Node 24), unit tests, end-to-end smoke and a11y. Artifacts retained.</li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">2 · Deploy</strong> runs only after CI succeeds. Site, app, subscribe and notch deploy in parallel via Wrangler. A running deploy is never cancelled mid-flight.</li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">3 · Commit hygiene</strong>: enforced conventional commits, with Release Please wired up for versioning and changelog.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Security -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>07 · Security</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Layered, not bolted on</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Branch protection on main requires every check below to pass before merge. Secrets live only in
          Cloudflare environment bindings, never in the repo.
        </p>

        <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-6">
          {securityChecks.map((c) => (
            <div class={`${cardClass} flex items-start gap-3`}>
              <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-[var(--color-accent-hi)] font-bold" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
              <span>
                <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)] block">{c.name}</strong>
                <span class="text-sm">{c.detail}</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Live security headers</p>
            <p class="text-sm">HSTS with preload and includeSubDomains. Strict CSP: frame-ancestors none, object-src none, base-uri self, form-action self, upgrade-insecure-requests. X-Frame-Options DENY, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy locking camera, microphone, geolocation, FLoC, topics, payment.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={cardClass}>
            <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Auth gates (app · GrowthHub)</p>
            <p class="text-sm">Cloudflare Pages Functions. HMAC-SHA256 signed cookies, timing-safe comparison, time-boxed tokens, rate-limited login. No credentials in source.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Resilience -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>08 · Resilience</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>Backup, failover, rollback</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mt-4">
          <div class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)] block mb-1">Backup</strong><span class="text-sm">Weekly mirror to Azure Static Web Apps as an independent cold standby.</span></div>
          <div class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)] block mb-1">Failover</strong><span class="text-sm">An operator-triggered workflow runs health checks, then flips DNS to the Azure standby via the Cloudflare API and restores it once the primary recovers.</span></div>
          <div class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)] block mb-1">Rollback</strong><span class="text-sm">Non-destructive git revert with no force-push, fully auditable, with a required reason.</span></div>
          <div class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)] block mb-1">Monitoring</strong><span class="text-sm">Daily production smoke (also fired by BetterStack incident webhooks), weekday status digest, weekly Lighthouse audit.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Agents -->
      <section>
        <p class={eyebrowClass}>09 · Operating model</p>
        <h2 class={h2Class}>A multi-agent build process</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Clear role separation with a defined handoff protocol.</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3">
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Claude Code</strong> · implementation: components, styling, templates, content collections, accessibility, SEO. Does not touch DNS, information architecture, positioning, or proof metrics without approval.</li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Codex</strong> · independent review: code, SEO, redirect maps, test scenarios, performance checklists. Closed tasks on separate branches.</li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">GPT-5.5 Thinking</strong> · strategy: positioning, page logic, trade-offs, the go / no-go release call.</li>
          <li class={cardClass}><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Claude Design</strong> · visual exploration only: variants and references, never the source of truth.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm">
          Handoff: strategy is written into docs, Claude implements against docs, Codex reviews independently,
          Wojciech accepts, and changes merge only once docs and implementation agree. Every page ships against a
          fixed Definition of Done: semantics, responsiveness, no placeholder copy, complete meta and OG, working
          CTAs, optimised images, reviewed accessibility, and validated proof claims.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
